  ("These feminine words can be applied to females: la trompeta = ‘trumpet’ or ‘female trumpet player’." 0.0920 0.9081 0.3980 0.4145 0.4145 0.0165 0.00482 0.4164 0.0493 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("1.2.10  Gender of names applied across sex boundaries" 0.0920 0.7260 0.4386 0.4594 0.4594 0.0208 0.00676 0.3105 0.0744 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0172 t nil 1)
  ("A female’s name applied to a male acquires masculine gender: tú eres un Margaret Thatcher ‘you’re" 0.0920 0.9082 0.4671 0.4836 0.4836 0.0165 0.00482 0.3851 0.0150 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("a Margaret Thatcher’ (said to a man of his right-wing political ideas). But men’s names usually" 0.0920 0.9081 0.4836 0.5001 0.5001 0.0165 0.00482 0.3510 0.0096 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("remain masculine: María, tú eres un Hitler con faldas ‘Maria, you’re a female Hitler’, lit. ‘Hitler with" 0.0920 0.9081 0.5001 0.5166 0.5166 0.0165 0.00482 0.4492 0.0599 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("skirts’." 0.0920 0.1487 0.5166 0.5331 0.5331 0.0165 nil 0.2327 0.0567 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("1.2.11  Nouns of invariable gender applied to either sex" 0.0920 0.7288 0.5572 0.5780 0.5780 0.0208 0.00676 0.3155 0.0744 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0172 t nil 1)
  ("Some common words applied to human beings do not change their gender. One says el bebé está" 0.0920 0.9081 0.5857 0.6021 0.6021 0.0165 0.00482 0.3443 0.0469 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("enfermo ‘the baby is ill’ whatever its sex, although la bebé or la bebe is nowadays commonly heard" 0.0920 0.9081 0.6021 0.6186 0.6186 0.0165 0.00482 0.3567 0.0642 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("for baby girl: una bebé muere al recibir un fármaco prescrito a su madre (El País, Sp.) ‘baby girl dies" 0.0920 0.9080 0.6187 0.6351 0.6351 0.0165 0.00482 0.2920 0.0245 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("after receiving drug prescribed for mother’ (la beba is heard in the Southern Cone). Some words" 0.0920 0.9081 0.6351 0.6516 0.6516 0.0165 0.00482 0.3148 0.0392 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("of common gender are:" 0.0920 0.2888 0.6516 0.6681 0.6681 0.0165 0.00482 0.3400 0.0169 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("el ángel angel" 0.1092 0.2198 0.6800 0.6965 0.6965 0.0165 0.00482 0.2807 0.0129 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("una calamidad calamity" 0.1092 0.3003 0.6965 0.7130 0.7130 0.0165 0.00482 0.3577 0.0300 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("una celebridad celebrity" 0.1092 0.3000 0.7130 0.7295 0.7295 0.0165 0.00482 0.2394 0.0300 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("un cerebrín genius/‘brainy’ person" 0.1092 0.4001 0.7295 0.7460 0.7460 0.0165 0.00482 0.2707 0.0214 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("un desastre disaster" 0.1092 0.2684 0.7460 0.7625 0.7625 0.0165 0.00482 0.2394 0.0214 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("un esperpento fright/weird-looking person" 0.1092 0.4665 0.7625 0.7790 0.7790 0.0165 0.00482 0.2871 0.0214 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("la estrella star (TV, etc.)" 0.1092 0.2991 0.7790 0.7955 0.7955 0.0165 0.00482 0.2816 0.0139 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("un genio genius" 0.1092 0.2385 0.7955 0.8120 0.8120 0.0165 0.00482 0.2839 0.0214 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("un ligue date/casual boy or girlfriend" 0.5233 0.8405 0.6800 0.6965 0.6965 0.0165 0.00482 0.2906 0.0214 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("una lumbrera genius" 0.5233 0.6901 0.6965 0.7130 0.7130 0.0165 0.00482 0.3013 0.0300 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("la pareja unmarried partner. See note 2" 0.5233 0.8461 0.7130 0.7295 0.7295 0.0165 0.00482 0.3285 0.0139 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("la persona person" 0.5233 0.6651 0.7295 0.7460 0.7460 0.0165 0.00482 0.2361 0.0139 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("el personaje character (in novels, etc.)" 0.5233 0.8302 0.7460 0.7625 0.7625 0.0165 0.00482 0.2710 0.0129 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("una pesadilla nightmare" 0.5233 0.7185 0.7625 0.7790 0.7790 0.0165 0.00482 0.3377 0.0300 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("(eres) un sol you’re wonderful/an angel" 0.5233 0.8563 0.7790 0.7955 0.7955 0.0165 0.00482 0.3083 0.0425 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("la víctima victim" 0.5233 0.6589 0.7955 0.8120 0.8120 0.0165 0.00482 0.3592 0.0139 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("and a few other masculine nouns can be used to refer to women, most of them, involving sexual" 0.0920 0.9080 0.8238 0.8403 0.8403 0.0165 0.00482 0.3637 0.0326 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("innuendo or comparisons with objects, cf. el pendón ‘trollop’/‘slut’ (lit. ‘pennant’, also la pendona)," 0.0920 0.9081 0.8404 0.8568 0.8568 0.0165 0.00482 0.3552 0.0824 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("el marimacho ‘tomboy’, etc." 0.0920 0.3153 0.8569 0.8733 0.8733 0.0165 0.00482 0.3918 0.0129 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(1)  Titles like Alteza ‘Highness’, Excelencia, Ilustrísima ‘Grace’ (title of bishops) and Majestad" 0.0920 0.9081 0.8855 0.9020 0.9020 0.0165 0.00482 0.3120 0.0273 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("‘Majesty’ are feminine, but the person addressed keeps his/her gender: Su Majestad estará cansado" 0.0920 0.9080 0.9020 0.9185 0.9185 0.0165 0.00482 0.3542 0.0775 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0))
  (20
  ("1.3 Group B: Gender of nouns referring to animals not included under 1.2 and to lifeless things 7" 0.1576 0.9088 0.0492 0.0683 0.0683 0.0154 0.00456 0.3600 0.0228 "UFSJES+Palatino-Light" 0.0129 nil nil 0)
  ("(to a king), ‘Your Majesty must be tired’. This particularly applies to the phrase su señoría used in" 0.0920 0.9080 0.0832 0.0997 0.0997 0.0165 0.00482 0.3542 0.0232 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("the Spanish parliaments to address other members of the two houses and for judges." 0.0920 0.8102 0.0997 0.1162 0.1162 0.0165 0.00482 0.3375 0.0267 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(2)  La pareja is used even for a male partner, but note su pareja es español (El Periódico, Sp., 8-3-15)" 0.0920 0.9080 0.1284 0.1449 0.1449 0.0165 0.00482 0.3165 0.0273 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("‘her (male) partner is Spanish’. Compañero/compañera are also used for unmarried partners," 0.0920 0.9080 0.1449 0.1613 0.1613 0.0165 0.00482 0.2611 0.0334 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("sometimes clarified by adding sentimental, but pareja is becoming more common." 0.0920 0.7750 0.1614 0.1778 0.1778 0.0165 0.00482 0.3765 0.0912 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("1.3  Group B: Gender of nouns referring to animals" 0.0920 0.7733 0.2061 0.2304 0.2304 0.0243 0.00789 0.3492 0.0474 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0201 t nil 1)
  ("not included under 1.2 and to lifeless things and" 0.1456 0.7954 0.2291 0.2533 0.2533 0.0243 0.00789 0.3055 0.0457 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0201 t nil 0)
  ("to plants" 0.1456 0.2655 0.2520 0.2763 0.2763 0.0243 0.00789 0.2979 0.0284 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0201 t nil 0)
