  ("la víbora viper" 0.6614 0.7783 0.4392 0.4557 0.4557 0.0165 0.00482 0.2797 0.0139 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("la vicuña vicuna" 0.6614 0.7952 0.4557 0.4722 0.4722 0.0165 0.00482 0.2939 0.0139 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("and many others which will be found in good dictionaries." 0.0920 0.5913 0.4844 0.5009 0.5009 0.0165 0.00482 0.3556 0.0326 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(1)  One can make an animal’s sex clear by adding macho ‘male’ or hembra ‘female’: la ardilla macho" 0.0920 0.9081 0.5131 0.5295 0.5295 0.0165 0.00482 0.3975 0.0273 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("‘male squirrel’, el cangrejo hembra ‘female crab’. In good Spanish, an adjective agrees with the" 0.0919 0.9080 0.5296 0.5461 0.5461 0.0165 0.00482 0.3000 0.0468 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("gender of the noun not of the animal itself: la rana macho está muerta ‘the male frog is dead’, un" 0.0919 0.9080 0.5461 0.5625 0.5625 0.0165 0.00482 0.3215 0.0597 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("cisne hembra blanco ‘a white female swan’. Macho and hembra are invariable: las cebras macho ‘male" 0.0919 0.9081 0.5626 0.5790 0.5790 0.0165 0.00482 0.3756 0.0389 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("zebras’, los gavilanes hembra ‘female sparrowhawks." 0.0920 0.5262 0.5791 0.5956 0.5956 0.0165 0.00482 0.3406 0.0651 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("Familiar language may say things like el/la gorila ‘he-gorilla’ and ‘she-gorilla’ (properly invariably" 0.0920 0.9081 0.6078 0.6242 0.6242 0.0165 0.00482 0.3572 0.0714 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("el gorila)." 0.0920 0.1658 0.6242 0.6407 0.6407 0.0165 0.00482 0.2308 0.0129 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("(2)  La canguro (‘she-kangaroo’) is used in Spain for a female child-minder or baby-sitter." 0.0920 0.8380 0.6529 0.6694 0.6694 0.0165 0.00482 0.3244 0.0273 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("1.3.2  Gender of nouns referring to non-living things, to plants" 0.0920 0.8085 0.6934 0.7142 0.7142 0.0208 0.00676 0.3257 0.0609 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0172 t nil 1)
  ("and to other animals" 0.1582 0.3989 0.7135 0.7343 0.7343 0.0208 0.00676 0.3493 0.0433 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0172 t nil 0)
  ("The gender of nouns referring to non-living things, to plants and to the animals mentioned" 0.0920 0.9081 0.7419 0.7584 0.7584 0.0165 0.00482 0.2607 0.0322 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("in 1.3.1 must be learned for each noun. It has no sexual implications and it sometimes varies" 0.0920 0.9081 0.7584 0.7749 0.7749 0.0165 0.00482 0.3029 0.0168 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("from place to place: cf. sauna ‘sauna’, feminine in Spain, either gender in Latin America; sartén" 0.0920 0.9080 0.7750 0.7914 0.7914 0.0165 0.00482 0.3254 0.0412 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("‘frying pan’/US ‘skillet’, feminine in Spain, often masculine in Latin America. The gender of" 0.0920 0.9081 0.7914 0.8079 0.8079 0.0165 0.00482 0.3220 0.0576 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("some nouns also occasionally changes with time: cf. seventeenth-century la puente, now el puente" 0.0920 0.9080 0.8079 0.8244 0.8244 0.0165 0.00482 0.3351 0.0449 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("‘bridge’ (occasionally still la puente in some regions). El maratón and la maratón ‘marathon’ are" 0.0920 0.9080 0.8244 0.8409 0.8409 0.0165 0.00482 0.3022 0.0663 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("both current nowadays: El País insists on el maratón." 0.0920 0.5315 0.8409 0.8574 0.8574 0.0165 0.00482 0.3317 0.0387 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("There are few infallible rules and we quote only those which in our view do not encourage false" 0.0920 0.9079 0.8696 0.8861 0.8861 0.0165 0.00482 0.3341 0.0487 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("generalizations." 0.0920 0.2266 0.8861 0.9026 0.9026 0.0165 nil 0.2293 0.1347 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0))
  (21
  ("8 Gender of nouns" 0.0905 0.2404 0.0492 0.0683 0.0683 0.0154 0.00456 0.3029 0.0124 "UFSJES+Palatino-Light" 0.0129 nil nil 0)
  ("1.3.3  Masculine by meaning" 0.0920 0.4191 0.0825 0.1033 0.1033 0.0208 0.00676 0.3875 0.0609 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0172 t nil 1)
  ("Some of these have acquired the gender of an underlying omitted noun:" 0.0920 0.7038 0.1110 0.1275 0.1275 0.0165 0.00482 0.3164 0.0469 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(a)  Rivers (el río): el Amazonas ‘the Amazon’, el Jarama, el Manzanares, el Sena ‘the Seine’, el Támesis" 0.0920 0.9080 0.1397 0.1562 0.1562 0.0165 0.00482 0.3920 0.0273 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("‘the Thames’, el Volga. Locally some rivers may be feminine, but outsiders rarely know this and" 0.0919 0.9080 0.1562 0.1727 0.1727 0.0165 0.00482 0.3507 0.0321 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("the masculine is always correct." 0.0919 0.3609 0.1727 0.1892 0.1892 0.0165 0.00482 0.3455 0.0267 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(b)  Mountains, oceans, seas and lakes (el monte, el océano, el mar, el lago): los Alpes, el Etna, el" 0.0919 0.9080 0.2014 0.2179 0.2179 0.0165 0.00482 0.3025 0.0294 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("Everest, el Himalaya (singular), el Pacífico, el Caribe ‘Caribbean’, el Windermere." 0.0919 0.7368 0.2179 0.2344 0.2344 0.0165 0.00482 0.3638 0.0622 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0)
  ("(c)  The names of cars, boats and aircraft (el coche, el barco, el avión): un Toyota, un Mercedes, el caza" 0.0919 0.9080 0.2466 0.2631 0.2631 0.0165 0.00482 0.3206 0.0262 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("‘fighter plane’, el Queen Elizabeth, el Marie Celeste, un DC10, un Mig-31. But small boats (la barca)" 0.0920 0.9080 0.2631 0.2796 0.2796 0.0165 0.00482 0.3617 0.0620 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("are usually feminine, as are light aircraft because of the noun la avioneta: una Cessna." 0.0920 0.8017 0.2796 0.2960 0.2960 0.0165 0.00482 0.3115 0.0261 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(d)  Months and days of the week (los meses y los días de la semana): enero/abril pasado, el lunes" 0.0920 0.9081 0.3083 0.3247 0.3247 0.0165 0.00482 0.2863 0.0294 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("‘Monday’, un viernes frío ‘a cold Friday’, etc." 0.0920 0.4636 0.3248 0.3412 0.3412 0.0165 0.00482 0.3657 0.0876 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(e)  Wines (el vino): el Borgoña ‘Burgundy’, el Chianti, un Rioja, el champaña ‘champagne’, usually el" 0.0920 0.9081 0.3534 0.3699 0.3699 0.0165 0.00482 0.3738 0.0273 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("champán in spoken Spanish, but la champaña in Mexico, Colombia and Venezuela. El cava is used" 0.0920 0.9081 0.3700 0.3864 0.3864 0.0165 0.00482 0.3293 0.0699 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("to refer to champagne made in Spain." 0.0920 0.4103 0.3865 0.4029 0.4029 0.0165 0.00482 0.3448 0.0168 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(f)  Pictures (el cuadro) by named artists: un Constable, un Leonardo, un Rembrandt, un Riley." 0.0920 0.8484 0.4151 0.4316 0.4316 0.0165 0.00482 0.3279 0.0251 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("(g)  Sports teams (el equipo): el Barça ‘Barcelona FC’ (pronounced [báɾ-sa]), el Betis (one of Seville’s" 0.0920 0.9081 0.4427 0.4606 0.4606 0.0165 0.00482 0.3313 0.0284 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
